                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "When I was little, I was able to play Cally's caves 3. It was a really amazing game and the gameplay was one of the most unique and is very inspiring to me. Years later, I want to be able to play them again. I find out that there was a 4th game, so I go to my phones play store, only to find out it doesn't work on my device. I then find out it's on steam and was on sale, so I go and buy it immediately. I open it ready to get nostalgic... After 10 minutes of playing, I was greatly disappointed in this game. First off, I enjoyed 3 since it had you go further to get power ups to then back track with those new power ups to get more stuff. In this game, you get EVERYTHING at the very beginning. The enemies also don't make any sense; why am I seeing a soccer player in the middle of a warzone or a library. Not to mention how most of them don't make any sense, why the heck is there just a missile that puts a giant red line across my screen? The only enemies that make sense are the ninjas in the ninja base level. I was so upset with this game that I actually quit playing it for about half a year to a full year. I've been trying to 100% games in my library, and finally decided to give this game one more go. I was so tired of this game until I got to the end of the regular game. Really well done story, I was actually glad I got this game. I just decided to continue to play, not just for the Blue Ribbon, but just because I miss when games didn't need to be extremely well done, they just need to be a game where a few people wanted to make a game. The story was really something and I'm glad I actually went through and played the game. Thank you so much for this game. (P.S: I would love to be a game tester for Cally's Caves 5, and I will definitely buy it when it comes out.)",
